{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 121, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading edge 0 to a 3x3 conv gives much larger gains (C100 +12) when the direct 0->3 edge is a skip rather than a conv or none."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "With a weak skip on edge 5, the 3x3 conv on edge 0 carries more of the representation, giving gains of about +15 versus about +4 with a conv on edge 5."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the 3x3 conv on edge 3 with a skip is harmful when edge 5 is also a skip, but neutral or positive when edge 5 is a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A strong 3x3 conv on edge 0 cushions the loss of the conv on edge 3, whereas with none, skip or avg_pool on edge 0 the swap costs several points."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Pooling on edge 4 is especially damaging when edge 3 is a skip (C100 -11.7), compared with about -2 when edge 3 is a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing edge 5 costs far less when edge 4 is a 3x3 conv, which keeps a strong path to the output."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 5 is catastrophic (IN16 -11.8) when edge 0 is already none, because the cell is left with few paths."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Dropping edge 1 when edge 2 is none removes the main route through node 1 and node 2, giving a large loss (IN16 -9.4)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a skip on edge 1 is roughly neutral or slightly positive, whereas removing a conv on edge 1 usually hurts."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "The gain from a 1x1 conv on edge 2 is smaller when edge 4 is already a strong 3x3 conv, and larger when edge 4 is none, skip or avg_pool."}], "tok": 33935, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "